    {
      "id": "w7v098g",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "SOURCES OF ENERGY"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Sun is the ultimate primary source of energy for almost all forms of energy on Earth, excluding nuclear, tidal, and geothermal energy.",
        "Conventional energy sources like coal and petroleum are exhaustible and contribute heavily to environmental pollution and acid rain.",
        "Solar cells are made of silicon semiconductors and convert sunlight directly into electrical energy via the photovoltaic effect.",
        "Nuclear power plants rely on controlled nuclear chain fission reactions of Uranium-235 or Plutonium-239 to produce thermal energy.",
        "Hydropower converts the potential energy of stored height-bound water into electrical energy without direct greenhouse gas emissions during operation."
      ],
      "id": "a01q0gw"
    },
